    "title": "BGSU women's basketball throttled by Ohio at home - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By BLADE STAFF ,\n2 hours ago\nBOWLING GREEN — After the first 10 minutes on Wednesday, Bowling Green women’s basketball kept it close against Ohio, finding itself down just 23-16.\nBy the time halftime rolled around, the Falcons did anything but keep it close, as a 23-7 second-quarter run by the Bobcats propelled them to eventually pick up a 25-point, 82-57 win over the Falcons at the Stroh Center.\nOU (12-5, 6-1 Mid-American Conference) were led by Bella Ranallo, who scored a game-high 26 points on 9-for-16 shooting. She finished a solid 6-for-9 behind the three-point line. Bobcat junior Bailey Tabeling nearly finished with a triple-double as she scored 20 points, grabbed eight boards, and dished out five assists. She was an efficient 6 of 7 from the floor and a perfect 7-for-7 from the free-throw line.\nThe Falcons, who fell to 10-9 (3-5 MAC), were led by Liberty-Benton graduate Lauren Gerken, who scored a team-best 10 points and had six rebounds. Ky'Aira Miller also had 10 points for BG.\nLosers of four of its last six, Bowling Green will look to turn the tide at 4 p.m. on Sunday, when it heads to Amherst, Mass., to take on Massachusetts.",
